<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Methodology</span></h2>

<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">III-A</span> </span><span id="S3.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">System Architecture</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We model an autonomous AI organization as a discrete-time system. At each time step <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, a task <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is presented to a group of <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> LLM agents. The system state <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> encodes agent roles, interaction topology, and accumulated organizational memory. The dynamics follow:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+1}=F(x_{t},u_{t},\tau_{t},w_{t},\varepsilon_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1}=F(x_{t},u_{t},\tau_{t},w_{t},\varepsilon_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> represents coordination decisions (protocol, routing), <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> captures external shocks (regulatory changes, agent failures, priority shifts), and <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> represents LLM stochasticity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">At each step, we measure five metrics:</p>
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}\in[0.25,1.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}\in[0.25,1.0]</annotation></semantics></math>: solution quality (multi-criteria LLM-as-judge);</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: execution time;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: cost (token consumption);</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: risk (compliance failures, errors);</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}\in[0.25,1.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}\in[0.25,1.0]</annotation></semantics></math>: mission relevance.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The optimization objective is:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\{u_{t}\}}J=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left(\alpha_{Q}Q_{t}+\alpha_{M}M_{t}-\alpha_{T}T_{t}-\alpha_{C}C_{t}-\alpha_{R}R_{t}\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\{u_{t}\}}J=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left(\alpha_{Q}Q_{t}+\alpha_{M}M_{t}-\alpha_{T}T_{t}-\alpha_{C}C_{t}-\alpha_{R}R_{t}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and constraints on acceptable risk and cost levels.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">III-B</span> </span><span id="S3.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Coordination Protocols: From Exogenous to Endogenous</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Four primary coordination protocols were evaluated, spanning a spectrum from fully <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">exogenous</span> (structure imposed externally) to fully <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">endogenous</span> (structure emerging from within):</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coordinator (centralized, exogenous):</span> Agent 0 acts as an external coordinator, analyzing the task and assigning roles and phases to all other agents, who execute in parallel. A single point of control determines the organizational structure. LLM calls: <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N+1</annotation></semantics></math> (1 sequential + <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> parallel).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sequential (hybrid):</span> Agents process the task in a fixed order. Each agent observes the <span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">completed outputs</span> of all predecessors and autonomously selects its role, decides whether to participate or abstain, and contributes accordingly. The ordering is exogenous, but role selection and participation decisions are fully <span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">endogenous</span>. LLM calls: <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> (sequential). This is analogous to a sports draft where each pick is informed by all previous selections.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Broadcast (signal-based, endogenous):</span> Two rounds—agents first broadcast role intentions simultaneously, then make final decisions informed by all intentions. LLM calls: <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2N</annotation></semantics></math> (parallel per round).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Shared (fully autonomous, endogenous):</span> Agents have access to a shared organizational memory (role history from previous tasks) and make all decisions simultaneously and independently. LLM calls: <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> (parallel).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Four additional bio-inspired protocols (Morphogenetic, Clonal, Stigmergic, Ripple) were also tested; their detailed results will be reported in a forthcoming companion paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">III-C</span> </span><span id="S3.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Task Complexity Levels</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tasks span four complexity levels:</p>
<ul id="S3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">L1 (Single-domain):</span> 1 domain, 3–5 steps, no dependencies (e.g., Application Programming Interface (API) security review);</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">L2 (Cross-domain):</span> 2 domains, 5–10 steps, knowledge integration required;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">L3 (Multi-phase):</span> 3+ domains, 10–20 steps, sequential dependencies between phases (e.g., zero-trust migration planning);</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">L4 (Adversarial):</span> 3+ domains with conflicting stakeholder interests, incomplete information, no single correct answer (e.g., CEO vs. Legal vs. CFO resource conflicts).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS4.6" class="ltx_text">III-D</span> </span><span id="S3.SS4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Evaluation Framework</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Quality assessment uses a multi-criteria <span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LLM-as-a-judge</span> methodology. An independent judge model—separate from the agent model to avoid self-evaluation bias—evaluates each solution across five dimensions on a 4-point scale with verbal anchors. The judge model was GPT-4o in Series 1–2 and GPT-5.4 in Series 3; within each series, the judge was held constant across all conditions:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Accuracy</span> (<math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\text{acc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\text{acc}}</annotation></semantics></math>): factual correctness;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completeness</span> (<math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\text{comp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>comp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\text{comp}}</annotation></semantics></math>): coverage of task requirements;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coherence</span> (<math id="S3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\text{coh}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>coh</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\text{coh}}</annotation></semantics></math>): logical consistency and structure;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Actionability</span> (<math id="S3.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\text{act}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>act</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\text{act}}</annotation></semantics></math>): readiness for practical application;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mission Relevance</span> (<math id="S3.I3.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\text{mis}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>mis</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\text{mis}}</annotation></semantics></math>): contribution to organizational mission.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Quality is aggregated as:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}=\frac{s_{\text{acc}}+s_{\text{comp}}+s_{\text{coh}}+s_{\text{act}}}{16},\quad Q_{t}\in[0.25,1.0]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>acc</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>comp</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>coh</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>act</mtext></msub></mrow><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}=\frac{s_{\text{acc}}+s_{\text{comp}}+s_{\text{coh}}+s_{\text{act}}}{16},\quad Q_{t}\in[0.25,1.0]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The lower bound of <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.25</annotation></semantics></math> arises because each sub-score has a minimum of <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> (not <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>) on the 4-point scale, so the minimum aggregate is <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4/16=0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4/16=0.25</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The evaluation methodology was iteratively refined through four versions (binary <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> 10-point <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> multi-criteria <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 4</annotation></semantics></math>) to achieve stable differentiation. The judge model changed between series (GPT-4o in Series 1–2, GPT-5.4 in Series 3); however, all cross-protocol and cross-model comparisons within each series use the <span id="S3.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">same</span> judge, ensuring internal validity. We acknowledge that inter-series comparisons should be interpreted with this caveat in mind.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">A Balance Index aggregates all metrics:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{t}=w_{Q}\hat{Q}_{t}+w_{M}\hat{M}_{t}+w_{T}\hat{T}_{t}+w_{C}\hat{C}_{t}+w_{R}\hat{R}_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{t}=w_{Q}\hat{Q}_{t}+w_{M}\hat{M}_{t}+w_{T}\hat{T}_{t}+w_{C}\hat{C}_{t}+w_{R}\hat{R}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\cdot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>⋅</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\cdot}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes normalized values and <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum w_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum w_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> (weights: <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{Q}=0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{Q}=0.25</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{M}=0.20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{M}=0.20</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{T}=0.20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{T}=0.20</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{C}=0.20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{C}=0.20</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{R}=0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{R}=0.15</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS5.6" class="ltx_text">III-E</span> </span><span id="S3.SS5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Experimental Design</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The experiment comprises three series (Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table II ‣ III-E Experimental Design ‣ III Methodology ‣ Drop the Hierarchy and Roles:How Self-Organizing LLM Agents Outperform Designed Structures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a>):</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE II: </span>Experimental design overview.</figcaption>
<table id="S3.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S3.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Series</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Focus</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Models</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Agents</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tasks</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S3.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">1</th>
<th id="S3.T2.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Foundational</th>
<td id="S3.T2.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">GPT-4o</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">4</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">660</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row">2</th>
<th id="S3.T2.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Scaling</th>
<td id="S3.T2.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">GPT-4.1-mini</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">4–64</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">8,020</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row">3</th>
<th id="S3.T2.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Multi-model</th>
<td id="S3.T2.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">8 LLMs</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">8–256</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">12,130</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"></th>
<th id="S3.T2.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Total</span></th>
<td id="S3.T2.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><math id="S3.T2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.T2.2.5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">20,810</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Series 1 (Foundation, 660 tasks):</span> Three coordination models were evaluated—Mean-Field Game (fixed roles, population-level coordination), Sparse Graph (topology-dependent coordination across complete, chain, and power-law networks), and Spectral Hierarchy (dynamically emergent hierarchy based on spectral analysis of agent contributions).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Series 2 (Scaling, 8,020 tasks):</span> Nine campaigns tested scaling from 4 to 64 agents across multiple topologies, complexity levels, and shock scenarios using GPT-4.1-mini.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Series 3 (Multi-model &amp; Protocols, 12,130 tasks):</span> Six blocks evaluated scaling to 256 agents, multi-model comparison (4 models), task complexity (L1–L4), evolutionary hybrids, organizational memory, and self-organizing roles across 4 closed/open-source models with multiple coordination protocols.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Shock resilience</span> was tested by introducing perturbations: random agent removal, hub agent removal, model substitution for 25% of agents, and regulatory/priority shifts.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reproducibility details.</span> All API-based models were accessed between February and March 2026 via official APIs or OpenRouter. Temperature was set to <math id="S3.SS5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.7</annotation></semantics></math> for agent models and <math id="S3.SS5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.0</annotation></semantics></math> for judge models to minimize evaluation variance. All prompts, configuration files, and run logs are preserved for reproducibility. We note that API-based models may be updated by providers over time; the exact model snapshots used are identified by run timestamps in our logs.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Results</span></h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Endogeneity Paradox: Protocol Determines Quality</span></h3>

<figure id="S4.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.28990v1/figures/fig5_protocols.png" id="S4.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/278;" width="476" height="278" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 1: </span>Quality comparison across coordination protocols. Solid bars: pilot (<math id="S4.F1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=8</annotation></semantics></math>, GPT-4.1-mini, L3+L4 average). Hatched bars: final (<math id="S4.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=16</annotation></semantics></math>, Claude Sonnet 4.6, L3). The hybrid Sequential protocol achieves the highest quality in both settings.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The direct comparison of four protocols under identical conditions (same agents, model, and tasks) revealed that the coordination mechanism has a decisive impact on solution quality—comparable to or exceeding the effect of model choice (Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table III ‣ IV-A The Endogeneity Paradox: Protocol Determines Quality ‣ IV Results ‣ Drop the Hierarchy and Roles:How Self-Organizing LLM Agents Outperform Designed Structures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE III: </span>Protocol comparison. Pilot: <math id="S4.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=8</annotation></semantics></math>, GPT-4.1-mini, average over L3+L4 tasks. Final (<math id="S4.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\text{L3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mtext>L3</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\text{L3}}</annotation></semantics></math>): <math id="S4.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=16</annotation></semantics></math>, Claude Sonnet 4.6, L3 tasks only.</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T3.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Protocol</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T3.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Type</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="S4.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\text{pilot}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mtext>pilot</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\text{pilot}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S4.T3.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="S4.T3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\text{L3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mtext>L3</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\text{L3}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S4.T3.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T3.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Balance</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.2.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T3.2.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Resilience</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T3.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Coordinator</th>
<th id="S4.T3.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Centralized</th>
<td id="S4.T3.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.640</td>
<td id="S4.T3.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.767</td>
<td id="S4.T3.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.478</td>
<td id="S4.T3.2.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.774</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="S4.T3.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sequential</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="S4.T3.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hybrid</span></th>
<td id="S4.T3.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T3.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.724</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T3.2.3.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.875</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T3.2.3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.510</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.2.3.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T3.2.3.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.829</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Broadcast</th>
<th id="S4.T3.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Signal-based</th>
<td id="S4.T3.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.510</td>
<td id="S4.T3.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">—</td>
<td id="S4.T3.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.363</td>
<td id="S4.T3.2.4.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.580</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Shared</th>
<th id="S4.T3.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Fully auton.</th>
<td id="S4.T3.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.503</td>
<td id="S4.T3.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">—</td>
<td id="S4.T3.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.369</td>
<td id="S4.T3.2.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.589</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The relative quality difference between the best (Sequential) and worst (Shared) protocol is <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="44\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>44</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">44\%</annotation></semantics></math>, with effect size Cohen’s <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1.86" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.86</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1.86</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.0001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.0001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.0001</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The paradox lies in the non-monotonic relationship between agent autonomy and quality: neither maximal external control (Coordinator—single point of failure) nor maximal autonomy (Shared—role duplication due to lack of real-time visibility) achieves optimality. The hybrid Sequential protocol succeeds because it provides agents with the optimal information type: not <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">intentions</span> (which may change, as in Broadcast), not <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">history</span> (which may be stale, as in Shared), not <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">someone else’s plan</span> (which may be suboptimal, as in Coordinator), but <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">completed outputs</span>—the factual results of predecessors in the current task.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-model replication.</span> The Sequential advantage over Coordinator was confirmed across all three tested strong models on L3 tasks (Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table IV ‣ IV-A The Endogeneity Paradox: Protocol Determines Quality ‣ IV Results ‣ Drop the Hierarchy and Roles:How Self-Organizing LLM Agents Outperform Designed Structures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
