</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span> </span><span id="S4.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Scaling: Sub-Linear Cost, Stable Quality</span></h3>

<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.28990v1/figures/fig3_scaling.png" id="S4.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/226;" width="476" height="226" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 2: </span>Scaling behavior in Series 2 (fixed roles, GPT-4.1-mini, <math id="S4.F2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=8\to 64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=8\to 64</annotation></semantics></math>). Quality remains stable (<math id="S4.F2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\in[0.949,0.955]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.949</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.955</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\in[0.949,0.955]</annotation></semantics></math>) while cost grows only <math id="S4.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11.8\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>11.8</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11.8\%</annotation></semantics></math> (coefficient of variation CV <math id="S4.F2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=4.4\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4.4</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=4.4\%</annotation></semantics></math>) despite an <math id="S4.F2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\times</annotation></semantics></math> increase in agents.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Scaling experiments across two series demonstrated remarkable stability.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Series 2 (fixed roles, <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=8\to 64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=8\to 64</annotation></semantics></math>, GPT-4.1-mini):</span> Quality remained virtually constant across an <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\times</annotation></semantics></math> increase in group size (Table <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table V ‣ IV-B Scaling: Sub-Linear Cost, Stable Quality ‣ IV Results ‣ Drop the Hierarchy and Roles:How Self-Organizing LLM Agents Outperform Designed Structures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">V</span></a>), with cost growing only <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11.8\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>11.8</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11.8\%</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE V: </span>Series 2 scaling (fixed roles, GPT-4.1-mini, 8,020 tasks).</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
